"cp":"Dvin's Muslim holders (the page does not name them)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamar_of_Georgia","c":2},{"y":1206,"t":"gain","x":"1206: David Soslan takes Kars.","cp":"saltukids","cpn":"Saltukids","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamar_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1225,"t":"contest_start","x":"1225: Jalal ad-Din attacks Georgia.","cp":"khwarezmid-empire","cpn":"Khwarazmian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalal_ad-Din_Mingburnu","c":2},{"y":1225,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1225: bridging entry, page silent.","cp":"shirvan","cpn":"Shirvan (Shirvanshahs)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalal_ad-Din_Mingburnu","c":1},{"y":1226,"t":"loss","x":"1226: Dvin is lost to the Khwarazmians.","cp":"khwarezmid-empire","cpn":"Khwarazmian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zakarid_Armenia","c":2},{"y":1231,"t":"contest_end","x":"15 August 1231: Jalal ad-Din is killed.","m":8,"cp":"khwarezmid-empire","cpn":"Khwarazmian Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalal_ad-Din_Mingburnu","c":2},{"y":1236,"t":"contest_start","x":"1236: Chormaqan invades Georgia.","cp":"mongol-empire","cpn":"Mongol Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1236,"t":"capital_move","x":"1236: bridging entry.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Georgia","c":1},{"y":1239,"t":"loss","x":"1239: the Mongols take Ani and Kars.","cp":"mongol-empire","cpn":"Mongol Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1239,"t":"loss","x":"1239: the Armenian princedoms pass to the Mongols.","cp":"mongol-empire","cpn":"Mongol Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zakarid_Armenia","c":2},{"y":1243,"t":"contest_end","x":"1243: Georgia submits to the Great Khan.","cp":"mongol-empire","cpn":"Mongol Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1259,"t":"split","x":"1259-1260: David VI Narin's revolt separates western Georgia.","cp":"kingdom-of-imereti","cpn":"Kingdom of Imereti","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Georgia","c":2},{"y":1266,"t":"loss","x":"1266: Samtskhe wins virtual independence.","cp":"samtskhe-saatabago","cpn":"Samtskhe-Saatabago","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Georgia","c":2},{"y":1327,"t":"contest_start","x":"1327: George V begins to free Georgia from the Ilkhanate.","cp":"ilkhanate","cpn":"Ilkhanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_V_of_Georgia","c":2},{"y":1330,"t":"merge","x":"1330: George V annexes Imereti and reunites Georgia.","cp":"kingdom-of-imereti","cpn":"Kingdom of Imereti","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1330,"t":"gain","x":"1330s: bridging entry, year not given.","cp":"ilkhanate","cpn":"Ilkhanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_V_of_Georgia","c":1},{"y":1334,"t":"gain","x":"1334: Samtskhe returns to the crown.","cp":"samtskhe-saatabago","cpn":"Samtskhe-Saatabago","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_V_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1335,"t":"contest_end","x":"1335: the Ilkhanate collapses.","cp":"ilkhanate","cpn":"Ilkhanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_V_of_Georgia","c":2},{"y":1357,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1357: the Jalayirids occupy Tiflis.","cp":"jalayirid-sultanate","cpn":"Jalayirid Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalayirid_Sultanate","c":2},{"y":1358,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1358: Tiflis is left.","cp":"jalayirid-sultanate","cpn":"Jalayirid Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalayirid_Sultanate","c":2},{"y":1386,"t":"contest_start","x":"22 November 1386: Timur takes Tbilisi.","m":11,"cp":"timurid-empire","cpn":"Timurid Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur%27s_invasions_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1387,"t":"contest_start","x":"1387: Alexander is crowned king of Imereti.","cp":"kingdom-of-imereti","cpn":"Kingdom of Imereti","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bagrat_V_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1389,"t":"contest_end","x":"1389: Bagrat V restores his suzerainty over Imereti.","cp":"kingdom-of-imereti","cpn":"Kingdom of Imereti","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bagrat_V_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1395,"t":"loss","x":"1395: bridging entry, the page does not say what Georgia lost.","cp":"timurid-empire","cpn":"Timurid Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur%27s_invasions_of_Georgia","c":1},{"y":1403,"t":"contest_end","x":"August 1403: Birtvisi falls and Georgia becomes Timur's tributary.","m":8,"cp":"timurid-empire","cpn":"Timurid Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur%27s_invasions_of_Georgia","c":2},{"y":1406,"t":"gain","x":"1406: George VII retakes Nakhchivan and Ganja.","cp":"timurid-empire","cpn":"Timurid Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur%27s_invasions_of_Georgia","c":2},{"y":1410,"t":"loss","x":"1410: Ganja and Nakhchivan are lost again.","cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","c":1},{"y":1414,"t":"gain","x":"1414: Alexander I subdues Samtskhe.","cp":"samtskhe-saatabago","cpn":"Samtskhe-Saatabago","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_I_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1431,"t":"gain","x":"1431: Alexander I retakes Lori.","cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_I_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1463,"t":"split","x":"1463: Chikhori breaks the kingdom.","cp":"kingdom-of-imereti","cpn":"Kingdom of Imereti","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Kartli","c":2},{"y":1463,"t":"loss","x":"1463: Samtskhe stands apart.","cp":"samtskhe-saatabago","cpn":"Samtskhe-Saatabago","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Kartli","c":2},{"y":1463,"t":"loss","x":"1463: bridging entry, page silent.","cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Kartli","c":1},{"y":1466,"t":"split","x":"1466: Kakheti becomes a kingdom.","cp":"kingdom-of-kakheti","cpn":"Kingdom of Kakheti","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Kakheti","c":3},{"y":1478,"t":"dissolve","x":"1478: the Georgian kingdom is divided in three.","cp":"kingdom-of-kartli","cpn":"Kingdom of Kartli","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Kartli","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Georgian-Byzantine war over Tao","from":1015,"to":1023,"outcome":"Byzantine victory: Basil II won at Shirimni on 11 September 1021; after the winter of 1022-1023 George I lost Tao, Javakheti, Shavsheti, the plains of Basiani, Artaani and Kola and fourteen fortresses.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_I_of_Georgia"},{"name":"Seljuk invasions of Georgia","from":1064,"to":1080,"outcome":"Alp Arslan came in 1064 and 1068 (Bagrat had to leave Kakheti for Kartli), Malik-Shah in 1076; from 1079/80 George II paid an annual tribute; the emir Ahmed took Kutaisi in 1080 (David IV page).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgian%E2%80%93Seljuk_wars"},{"name":"Georgian reconquest from the Seljuks","from":1099,"to":1124,"outcome":"Georgian victory: no tribute from 1099; Trialeti 1110, Rustavi 1115, Lori 1118, Botora (February 1120), Didgori (12 August 1121), Tbilisi (February 1122), Dmanisi (March 1124).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_IV_of_Georgia"},{"name":"Georgian-Shirvan war","from":1123,"to":1130,"outcome":"David IV invaded in June 1123 and recovered Shamakhi in September 1124; after Manuchihr's return (1125) and a rebellion (1126) Demetrius settled in 1129-30 on a border at the Tetritsqali, eastern Shirvan under Manuchihr as Georgian vassal.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demetrius_I_of_Georgia"},{"name":"Wars for Ani","from":1124,"to":1199,"outcome":"Ani passed from the Shaddadids to David IV (1124), back to them as a vassal (1130), to George III (1161), out (1164), in again (1174) and finally to Zakare for Georgia (c.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgian%E2%80%93Seljuk_wars"},{"name":"Tamar's wars against the Eldiguzids, Rum and Erzurum","from":1191,"to":1209,"outcome":"Georgian gains: Shirvan tributary (early 1190s), Shamkor (1195), Basian (1202, 1203 or 1204), Dvin (1203-1205), Kars (1206); in 1209 Georgia besieged Khlat and raided Ardabil, Marand, Tabriz and Qazvin without annexing.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamar_of_Georgia"},{"name":"Khwarazmian conquest of Georgia","from":1225,"to":1231,"outcome":"Jalal ad-Din beat the Georgians at Garni (1225) and took Tbilisi (1225 on this page, 1226 on the Mongol page); Dvin was lost in 1226-1230 while Ani and Kars held; he was killed on 15 August 1231.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalal_ad-Din_Mingburnu"},{"name":"Mongol invasions of Georgia","from":1220,"to":1243,"outcome":"The raids of 1220-1221 were followed by the conquest of 1236-1243: Ivane submitted in 1238, Ani and Kars fell in 1239, Georgia acknowledged the Great Khan in 1243 and paid tribute.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Georgia"},{"name":"Georgian rebellion against the Ilkhanate","from":1259,"to":1260,"outcome":"Georgian nobles under David Narin rose in 1259-1260; the page gives no outcome and no territorial change.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Georgia"},{"name":"George V's liberation from Ilkhanid rule","from":1327,"to":1335,"outcome":"Georgia stopped paying tribute and expelled the Mongol army between 1327 and 1335; the Mongols mounted further campaigns in the 1330s and 1340s 'with no success'.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_V_of_Georgia"},{"name":"Timur's invasions of Georgia","from":1386,"to":1403,"outcome":"Timur took Tbilisi on 22 November 1386, returned in 1387, 1388, 1394, 1399, 1400 and 1401 and captured Birtvisi in August 1403; Georgia became his tributary but kept its independence, and George VII regained Nakhchivan and Ganja in 1406 (lost again by 1410 on…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur%27s_invasions_of_Georgia"},{"name":"Reconquest of Lori","from":1431,"to":1431,"outcome":"Alexander I re-conquered Lori 'from the Turkomans' in 1431; c.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_I_of_Georgia"},{"name":"Jahan Shah's invasion of Georgia","from":1440,"to":1440,"outcome":"After Alexander refused tribute, Jahan Shah destroyed Samshvilde and sacked Tbilisi in March 1440; no land changed hands.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_I_of_Georgia"},{"name":"Collapse of the kingdom: Chikhori to the tripartite division","from":1463,"to":1478,"outcome":"George VIII was beaten at Chikhori (1463) and captured (1465); Bagrat VI proclaimed himself king of all Georgia in 1466; the realm divided into Kartli (1478), Imereti and Kakheti, with the de jure end in 1490.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Kartli"}],"certainty":[{"from":1008,"to":1478,"level":"soft","note":"Medieval frontiers are described by cities and provinces, not lines; the only fixed line on the pages is the Tetritsqali border in Shirvan from 1129-30."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Georgia","title":"Kingdom of Georgia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_IV_of_Georgia","title":"David IV of Georgia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgian%E2%80%93Seljuk_wars","title":"Georgian-Seljuk wars"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamar_of_Georgia","title":"Tamar of Georgia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_invasions_of_Georgia","title":"Mongol invasions of Georgia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalal_ad-Din_Mingburnu","title":"Jalal ad-Din Mingburnu"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_V_of_Georgia","title":"George V of Georgia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur%27s_invasions_of_Georgia","title":"Timur's invasions of Georgia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_I_of_Georgia","title":"Alexander I of Georgia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demetrius_I_of_Georgia","title":"Demetrius I of Georgia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_I_of_Georgia","title":"George I of Georgia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Kartli","title":"Kingdom of Kartli"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bagrat_V_of_Georgia","title":"Bagrat V of Georgia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zakarid_Armenia","title":"Zakarid Armenia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basil_II","title":"Basil II"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Javakheti","title":"Javakheti"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bagrat_IV_of_Georgia","title":"Bagrat IV of Georgia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samtskhe-Saatabago","title":"Samtskhe-Saatabago"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Kakheti","title":"Kingdom of Kakheti"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalayirid_Sultanate","title":"Jalayirid Sultanate"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","title":"Qara Qoyunlu"}]}